City National's authoritative standard for writing and reviewing job descriptions. Covers what each JD section means and must contain (Purpose, Principal Duties and Responsibilities, People Management, Sales, Relationship Manager, NMLS, Education, Work Experience, Certifications and Licenses, Knowledge Skills and Abilities), house writing style, approved education and experience options, the 2+ direct reports rule, Individual Contributor levels (I, II, III, Senior, Lead), people-leadership tiers (Team Leader, Supervisor, Manager, Director), title families (Administrator, Coordinator, Specialist, Analyst) and the Analyst reality check, cross-section consistency checks, HR review flags, and how HR runs a new-position intake. Use for any question about how JDs, titles, levels, or JD wording work, for both new positions and updates. Takes precedence over wording found in existing job descriptions.

For update-specific formatting rules, follow JD_Update_Quality_Guide.md.
